# basePath DesignDoubleDepletion
// Double Depletion

::Intro
@trigger    OnDesignSetupComplete
$set temp:hintGiven = 0
{@PAL} Take a look at that Verification Table! Two outputs, and they need different signals.

::Hints
@trigger    OnSingleTestComplete
@when       result == "failure"
$if temp:hintGiven == 0
    {@PAL}  <color=yellow>Hint:</color> Check the Verification Table. When A is HI, block Y. When B is LO, block X.
    $set temp:hintGiven = 1
$elseif temp:hintGiven == 1
    {@PAL}  <color=yellow>Hint:</color> You will need two Gates. One closes with HI, one closes with LO.
    $set temp:hintGiven = 2
$elseif temp:hintGiven == 2
    {@PAL}  <color=yellow>Hint:</color> A connects to X, but is blocked by LO B. B connects to Y, but is blocked by HI A.
    $set temp:hintGiven = 0
$endif